-- gap[067]. A numeric `for` whose body's ONLY effect is a CALL.
--
-- `--backend=direct` used to drop the loop entirely: `for i = 1, 3 / print(i)`
-- printed `1 2 3` under the C backend and NOTHING under the direct one. Both
-- printed `ok compile`, both exited 0, and no diagnostic was emitted — the
-- numeric-`for` liveness computed body liveness from DATA reaching an
-- observable, and a call did not count as an effect, so the trip count folded
-- away. `while` with the identical body was always correct, which is why the
-- defect read as a `for` lowering bug rather than a general one.
--
-- THIS FILE IS ONLY A GATE BECAUSE STDOUT IS COMPARED. Every row below exits 0
-- on both backends and differs only in what it PRINTS, so for as long as
-- `native_differential` compared exit status alone it was structurally unable
-- to see any of them. The comparison and the fixtures land together; either
-- one without the other is theatre.
--
-- `control` is the positive control: it proves the harness can report
-- agreement, so an empty `direct` column would be a real absence.

-- A user-defined callee, to show the defect is not about `print` specifically.
shout(v: i64): i64
    print(v)
    0

bare(): i64
    for i = 1, 3
        print(i)
    0

stepped(): i64
    for i = 1, 3, 1
        print(i)
    0

viafn(): i64
    for i = 1, 3
        shout(i)
    0

nested(): i64
    for i = 1, 2
        for j = 1, 2
            print(j)
    0

-- Positive control: the same body under `while`, which was never wrong.
control(): i64
    i = 1
    while i <= 3
        print(i)
        i = i + 1
    0

-- Accumulating into a value the caller observes always kept the loop; kept
-- here so a fix that deletes the loop for a DIFFERENT reason still fails.
summed(): i64
    s = 0
    for i = 1, 3
        s = s + i
    s

main(): i64
    bare()
    stepped()
    viafn()
    nested()
    control()
    -- 6, and the exit status carries it so a stdout-only regression is not the
    -- only thing this file can catch.
    summed()
